'''''Nephrolepis brownii''''', the '''Asian sword fern''',<ref name="volcanos-park-ferns" >{{cite web | title=Ferns | website = Hawaiʻi Volcanoes National Park | url = https://www.nps.gov/havo/learn/nature/ferns.htm | access-date=2022-06-14 }}</ref><ref name="plants">{{cite web | url = https://plants.usda.gov/home/plantProfile?symbol=NEMU | website = USDA PLANTS | title = Nephrolepis multiflora (Roxb.) Jarrett ex Morton}}</ref> is a species of fern native to Asia and introduced elsewhere.<ref name="flora-china">{{cite web | title = Nephrolepis brownii | work = Flora of China | url = http://www.efloras.org/florataxon.aspx?flora_id=2&taxon_id=250098741 }}</ref> It is a perennial herb<ref>{{Cite web |title=The Institute for Regional Conservation |url=https://www.regionalconservation.org/ircs/database/plants/PlantPageFK.asp?TXCODE=Nephbrow |access-date=2025-03-10 |website=www.regionalconservation.org}}</ref> and grows up to {{Convert|3|ft|m|abbr=on}} tall.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Plant Details - FLIP |url=https://plantatlas.usf.edu/flip/plant.aspx?id=51 |access-date=2025-03-10 |website=plantatlas.usf.edu}}</ref>

==Range==

The native range includes most of southeast Asia and extends north to China and Japan, west to Sri Lanka and India, east to Pacific islands, and south to Australia.<ref name="flora-china" /> It is introduced in North and South America<ref name="flora-china" /> and Hawaii.<ref name="volcanos-park-ferns" /><ref name="flora-north-america">{{cite web | url = http://www.efloras.org/florataxon.aspx?flora_id=1&taxon_id=233500799 | work = Flora of North America | title = Nephrolepis multiflora}}</ref><ref name="plants" />

